<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 3.378 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 3.378 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 3.378  billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination  of three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements, dealers  said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered as follows:</p>
<p>	AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>	150 million    363 days</p>
<p>	150 million    181 days</p>
<p>	150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered  as follows:</p>
<p>	500 million     42 days</p>
<p>	600 million     41 days</p>
<p>	600 million     28 days</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     20 days</p>
<p>	228 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
